  "final_text": "Both objects exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data exploration.** The data view `kibana_sample_data_logs` has 47 fields. The ones that matter here are `@timestamp` (time field), `response` (string, with a `response.keyword` subfield for exact match), `bytes` (number), `clientip` (ip), `geo.dest`, `extension`, `machine.os`, and `url`. I couldn't pull actual value counts: the ES|QL, console proxy, and internal search endpoints return 404 or \"not available\" on this Kibana, so I relied on the field metadata.\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-80a30255 Web logs overview`** (id `13a021e9-bf83-4036-b32e-0117e7c717f1`), six panels:\n- A markdown header.\n- Metric: Total requests (count).\n- Metric: 5xx responses (count, with a DSL filter `response.keyword: 5*`).\n- Metric: Total bytes served (sum of `bytes`).\n- Line chart: Requests over time (date histogram on `timestamp`).\n- Bar chart: Responses by status code (terms on `response.keyword`, top 10).\n\nThe first save dropped the 5xx filter's query. I fixed it with a PUT and read the panels back to confirm.\n\n**Rule: `EFF-80a30255 5xx spike`** (id `c09aee12-310b-4900-bf66-06189822dfd3`):\n- Type: Elasticsearch query rule, KQL search on the data view.\n- Query: `response.keyword : 5*`.\n- Schedule: every 1 minute.\n- Window: 5 minutes, count, grouped across all documents.\n- Condition: fires when count > 10.\n- Enabled, with execution status `ok`.\n\n**Choices I made:**\n- \"5xx\" means any status code starting with 5, matched with a wildcard on `response.keyword`.\n- I added the tag `EFF-80a30255` to the rule and set `excludeHitsFromPreviousRun: true` so each window's hits aren't double-counted.\n- The rule has no actions, so it will evaluate and log but won't notify anyone. Tell me if you want a connector attached.",
